{
  "description": "The four ways the historical importer refuses to drop a snapshot line it cannot turn into an observation: an unmapped record kind (with and without a timestamp of its own), a record of a mapped kind that is missing a field that kind requires, and a line that is not JSON at all. Each becomes a dev.cclog.source.gap.v1 marker instead of vanishing. This is by far the highest-volume event class the importer emits, so its exact shape is pinned here rather than left to a hand check.",
  "exercises": [
    "integrity event (source.gap) as produced by the historical importer, not the collector",
    "reason distinguishes unmapped_kind / missing_field / parse_error",
    "time_basis distinguishes real activity time from archive-acquisition time",
    "detail is a short validated label, never source content",
    "marker identity is snapshot digest + line number, so a re-run collapses onto it"
  ],
